<!--
    Copyright (c) 2026 Splitwirez
    Licensed under the MIT License. See LICENSE-aero-theme-for-avalonia.txt in the Themes/Aero
    directory for the full text of the copyright notice and permission notice.
    Source: https://github.com/Splitwirez/aero-theme-for-avalonia at main = a705b7c0
            src/AeroAvalonia/ControlStyles/ProgressBar.axaml
    Changes from upstream: this file is the DETERMINATE BRANCH of a 471-line, 26,806-byte original.
    Every line below is upstream's, byte for byte, except the four changes 1, 8, 9 and 10 record;
    what makes the file short is what was left OUT, and that is enumerated here rather than
    summarised.
    (Upstream's own indentation is 4 spaces on this file where the other vendored ControlStyles use
    tabs; it is kept, because keeping it is what lets the retained lines be compared verbatim.)
      1. RE-POINTED the aeconv xmlns from "using:AeroAvalonia.Converters" to
         "using:TanMenu.Wpf.Themes.Aero.Converters".
      2. DROPPED ControlTheme x:Key="ProgressBarAnimation" (upstream :144-214) and
         x:Key="ProgressBarGlowPattern" (:43-139) whole, the four glow-mask LinearGradientBrushes
         (:11-38) that only those two consumed, and the TemplatedControl x:Name="BarAnimation"
         (:260-268) that instantiated the first from inside the main template. That is the
         indeterminate machinery; this app never sets IsIndeterminate on anything
         ("grep -rn IsIndeterminate src tests" finds only prose), and the design's Task 5 rules the
         determinate case the only one it will ship.
      3. DROPPED Panel x:Name="IndeterminateRoot" (:257-259 — an EMPTY Panel whose IsVisible was the
         negation of DeterminateRoot's) and the ^:indeterminate / ^:not(:indeterminate) style blocks
         (:430-450) that were the rest of the same machinery.
      4. DROPPED the nine dead style rules the design's §5.5 enumerates: :309, :312, :320, :335
         (horizontal) and :363, :366, :374, :389 (vertical) target Border#IndeterminateProgressBarIndicator
         and Border#IndeterminateProgressBarIndicator2, and :442 targets Control#GlowClipHelper.
         NONE of those three names is declared anywhere in the upstream file, so all nine matched
         nothing upstream too. §5.5 also lists ":156, a {Binding #GlowClipHelper.Bounds} to a name
         that does not exist" as a tenth defect; it is not one — upstream :156 sits inside the XML
         comment that opens at :152 and closes at :158, so it never bound anything either way. It
         goes with change 2 regardless.
      5. DROPPED ControlTheme x:Key="StorageBar" (:454-470). It is keyed by name, so nothing reaches
         it implicitly, and no control in this app asks for it. Two of the three brushes it named
         (AeroProgressBarStorageFrameBackground, AeroProgressBarStorageFrameInnerBorderBrush) stay in
         the vendored AVMAP/Brushes.axaml, which was taken whole for the reason Task 2 recorded.
      6. DROPPED LayoutTransformControl x:Name="PART_LayoutTransformControl" with its
         TextBlock#ProgressText (:272-284), the ^[ShowProgressText=True] block (:408-427), and the
         StringFormatConverter (:7) those alone consumed. CONSEQUENCE, stated rather than
         discovered: ShowProgressText="True" now renders no text at all. Nothing in this app sets it
         (it defaults to false), and dropping the part throws nothing — Avalonia 12.1's ProgressBar
         declares exactly one required part, [TemplatePart("PART_Indicator", typeof(Border),
         IsRequired = true)], and its OnApplyTemplate resolves that one name and no other with
         NameScope.Get<Border> (decompiled from Avalonia.Controls 12.1.0 with ilspycmd).
      7. DROPPED the EnumToBoolConverter (:8) and ProgressBarFillColorConverter (:9) resource
         instances with their last consumers, and DELETED Converters/ProgressBarAnimationConverter.cs
         and Converters/ProgressBarFillColorConverter.cs from this vendoring for the same reason.
         ProgressBarFillBrushConverter.cs stays: the indicator's fill below is its one live call site.
      8. DROPPED Panel x:Name="DeterminateRoot" (:237-238), the wrapper whose whole job was to be
         switched off by the ^:indeterminate rule of change 3. PART_Indicator is now a direct child
         of the same Panel that already held it and ShineBorder as siblings, one level up, and the
         twelve lines of its subtree are de-indented by four spaces to match — the only whitespace
         edit in the file. Diffed line by line against the upstream copy, exactly three things below
         are not byte-identical to it: this de-indent, change 1's xmlns and change 9's two bindings.
         The geometry is unchanged: ProgressBar.UpdateIndicator sizes the indicator against
         _indicator.VisualParent.Bounds, and both panels fill InnerBorder's content box exactly.
      9. CONVERTED ShineBorder's two {ReflectionBinding}s (:255-256) to
         {Binding #PART_Indicator.Bounds.Width|Height, Mode=OneWay} — the idiom the same element's
         Margin already used two lines above. Those two were the whole port's only reflection
         bindings, so the tree now has none.
     10. DROPPED ShineBorder's CornerRadius binding (:254). It read
         CornerRadius="{Binding #PART_Indicator.Margin, Mode=OneWay}" — the indicator's MARGIN, a
         Thickness, assigned to a CornerRadius — one line below the Margin binding it was evidently
         copied from. It COMPILES (this file was built with it in place, 0 warnings) and it cannot
         ever produce a value: Avalonia.Utilities.TypeUtilities.TryConvert's last four fallbacks are
         the target's TypeConverter, the source's TypeConverter, an implicit conversion operator and
         an explicit one, and Thickness declares no operator to CornerRadius, CornerRadius declares
         none from Thickness, and neither struct carries a [TypeConverter] that knows the other
         (all four decompiled from Avalonia.Base 12.1.0). The binding therefore fails at run time on
         every ProgressBar and leaves CornerRadius at its 0,0,0,0 default. A binding that provably
         cannot resolve is the same class of defect as a selector that provably cannot match, so it
         is dropped rather than carried; ShineBorder draws square corners, which is what it drew
         upstream.

    ── What the template draws, and where its numbers come from ─────────────────────────────────
    Two nested 1 px frames, radius 3 outside and 2 inside, over a vertical trough gradient; the
    indicator is a third radius-1 rounded rectangle inside them. THAT is why the design re-values
    both consumers' Height from 4 to 15: at 4 DIP the two frames and the indicator's own corner
    radius consume the whole bar and nothing reads as a fill. 15 is PUBLISHED —
    https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/uxguide/vis-layout gives a progress bar as
    "160 or 355 x 15 relative pixels" — and it is above the MinHeight of 13 this theme sets, so it
    is the control's own layout that grows rather than a local value fighting the theme.

    ShineBorder is the glass gloss and it STRETCHES ACROSS THE WHOLE TRACK, filled or not: its
    AeroProgressBarHorizontalShine is a top-to-bottom brush whose stops go white -> white -> hard
    Transparent at the midpoint, so it whitens the upper half of the trough and the upper half of
    the fill alike. The MinWidth/MinHeight bindings of change 9 do not confine it — a Border in a
    Panel stretches past its minimum on its own — and upstream's only consumer of that confinement
    was the StorageBar theme of change 5, which added the matching MaxWidth. They are kept, at the
    design's instruction, because converting them is what takes the reflection-binding count to zero.
-->
<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:aeconv="using:TanMenu.Wpf.Themes.Aero.Converters"
    x:ClassModifier="internal">

    <ControlTheme x:Key="{x:Type ProgressBar}" TargetType="ProgressBar">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource AeroProgressBarFrameBackground}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource AeroProgressBarFrameOuterBorderBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource AeroProgressBarFill}" />
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
        <Setter Property="Template">
            <ControlTemplate>
                <Border x:Name="ProgressBarRoot"
                        BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                        BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                        CornerRadius="3">
                    <Border x:Name="InnerBorder"
                            Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                            BorderBrush="{DynamicResource AeroProgressBarFrameInnerBorderBrush}"
                            BorderThickness="1"
                            CornerRadius="2"
                            ClipToBounds="True">
                        <Panel>
                            <Border x:Name="PART_Indicator"
                                    Margin="{TemplateBinding Padding}"
                                    CornerRadius="1"
                                    ClipToBounds="True">
                                <Border.Background>
                                    <MultiBinding Converter="{x:Static aeconv:ProgressBarFillBrushConverter.Instance}">
                                        <TemplateBinding Property="Foreground" />
                                        <TemplateBinding Property="Orientation" />
                                        <DynamicResource ResourceKey="AeroProgressBarFillFallback" />
                                    </MultiBinding>
                                </Border.Background>
                            </Border>
                            <Border x:Name="ShineBorder"
                                    Margin="{Binding #PART_Indicator.Margin, Mode=OneWay}"
                                    MinWidth="{Binding #PART_Indicator.Bounds.Width, Mode=OneWay}"
                                    MinHeight="{Binding #PART_Indicator.Bounds.Height, Mode=OneWay}" />
                        </Panel>
                    </Border>
                </Border>
            </ControlTemplate>
        </Setter>

        <Style Selector="^:horizontal">
            <Setter Property="MinWidth" Value="100" />
            <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="13" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center" />

            <Style Selector="^ /template/ Border#PART_Indicator">
                <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Left" />
                <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^ /template/ Border#ShineBorder">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource AeroProgressBarHorizontalShine}" />
            </Style>
        </Style>


        <Style Selector="^:vertical">
            <Setter Property="MinWidth" Value="13" />
            <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="100" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Center" />

            <Style Selector="^ /template/ Border#PART_Indicator">
                <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
                <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Bottom" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^ /template/ Border#ShineBorder">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource AeroProgressBarVerticalShine}" />
            </Style>
        </Style>
    </ControlTheme>
</ResourceDictionary>
